# URL of the LabourLink API (server/). Leave this unset for local dev AND for
# the deployed browser/PWA build — with no VITE_API_URL, the frontend targets
# whatever host the page was loaded from (see web/src/lib/api.ts), which
# works correctly whether that's localhost, a phone hitting this machine's
# LAN IP for real-device testing, or the production web origin (which then
# proxies /api/* to the real API service server-side — see the API_URL note
# in web/serve-static.js and the README's Railway deploy section). Setting
# this makes every browser request target the API's own cross-site origin
# directly instead, which Safari's cross-site cookie blocking (ITP) silently
# breaks login for — see README.md. The ONLY place this should ever be set
# is the Android build's env files (web/.env.android*): a native WebView has
# no same-origin proxy in front of it, so it needs the real API URL
# directly. web/vite.config.ts fails the plain browser production build hard
# if this is set, specifically to catch that mistake early.
# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:4000

# Runtime-only (NOT VITE_-prefixed, so Vite never inlines it into the
# browser bundle) pointer to the API service, read by web/serve-static.js in
# production to proxy /api/* requests server-side. Not used in local dev
# (the dev server needs no proxy — see VITE_API_URL's comment above). Set
# only as an actual Railway env var on the web service, never in this file.
# API_URL=https://<api-service>.up.railway.app

# --- Supabase project credentials ---
# Not currently read by web code, but reserved for future use of the
# Supabase client. Publishable key is safe for client-side use; project URL
# only — do not append /rest/v1 or any other path.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# IANA timezone the greenhouse operates in — must match the server's
# APP_TIMEZONE. Used by the desktop Inputs page for date defaults, day
# navigation, and end-time correction input. Optional — defaults to
# "America/Toronto" if unset.
# VITE_APP_TIMEZONE=America/Toronto

# --- Web Push (installed PWA / iPhone Home Screen) ---
# The PUBLIC half of the VAPID keypair generated for server/.env's
# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY/VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY — must be the exact same public key on
# both sides. Safe to expose to the client; this is not a secret. Without
# it, SettingsScreen's "Enable notifications" button shows a clear
# "not configured" message instead of attempting a subscription.
VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
